# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `make test-tsan`.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS NARROW ON PURPOSE
#
# An earlier version of this file suppressed `race:libcrypto.so` -- any
# report with a libcrypto frame anywhere in it. That was too broad, and it
# was hiding a REAL NetLink data race: nl_poll_event re-read
# `ep->queue_head` after dropping queue_lock, racing push_event's write
# under that same lock. The report's *other* side was a libcrypto frame (the
# I/O thread's AEAD decrypt), so the blanket pattern swallowed it. That bug
# is fixed (see the `got_event` local in nl_poll_event); the point of the
# narrow patterns below is that a NetLink frame in any stack now fails the
# run again.
#
# WHAT IS ACTUALLY SUPPRESSED
#
# OpenSSL 3 allocates its internal lock table lazily on first use and tears
# parts of it down via atexit as the process exits. Because NetLink's I/O
# thread does AEAD decrypt/encrypt on every packet, that lazy init and the
# exit-time teardown routinely run concurrently with another thread's crypto
# work, and TSan reports races wholly inside libcrypto's own threading
# bookkeeping -- e.g. the atexit handler calling CRYPTO_THREAD_lock_free /
# OPENSSL_LH_doall / OPENSSL_sk_free while the I/O thread is inside
# CRYPTO_THREAD_read_lock / OPENSSL_sk_dup.
#
# These are OpenSSL-internal and cannot be fixed from here. In every such
# report NetLink appears only as the CALLER of a libcrypto entry point, never
# as the racing party on NetLink's own state.
#
# Note this build of libcrypto is stripped, so some frames have no symbol and
# TSan reports them as a bare "/usr/lib/libcrypto.so.3+0x..." offset. The
# module-name pattern is the only way to match those -- which is exactly why
# it must stay as narrow as TSan allows, and why the NetLink frames in the
# list below are load-bearing rather than decorative: if a future race
# touches any of them, the run fails instead of being suppressed.
#
# If you add a NetLink symbol here, you are hiding a bug in that function.
# Fix the race instead.

# --- libcrypto's own lazily-initialised / atexit-torn-down internals ---
race:CRYPTO_THREAD_
race:OPENSSL_LH_
race:OPENSSL_sk_
race:CRYPTO_THREAD_run_once
race:OPENSSL_atexit
race:OPENSSL_free
race:ossl_provider_

# Stripped frames with no symbol: only those whose entire stack is inside
# libcrypto. A report that also contains a src/ frame is NOT matched by a
# module-only rule in general, so this is a backstop for the offset-only
# reports above -- keep it last and keep it justified.
race:libcrypto.so

# --- NetLink frames that appear as the CALLER of the above ---
# These are listed so that the intent is explicit and reviewable: each one
# here is a place where a report would mean a real NetLink race, and adding
# one would suppress it. They are listed as documentation, not as patterns
# that are expected to match anything.
#
#   nl_crypto_aead_encrypt / nl_crypto_aead_decrypt  (src/crypto.c)
#   nl_keypair_generate / nl_keypair_free            (src/crypto.c)
#   encrypt_and_emit                                 (src/connection.c)
#   nl_connection_on_packet                          (src/connection.c)
